ause it was hard to feel good will for them while actually there, as Levi does not like crowds.<br /> <br /> But I'm growing more appreciative of festivals as a form of cultural expression and general release.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T06:24:47-07:00","id":93434,"title":"","content":"What is St. Patrick's Day about, anyway? I almost got into a fight with my boss about the whole Guiness boycott of the New York parade over the exclusion of gay floats when she said, &quot;It's not about that,&quot; because I wanted to snap, &quot;Why, there aren't gay Irish people?&quot; Then I realized she might actually be right, as I have no idea what the holiday celebrates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T06:51:31-07:00","id":93450,"title":"","content":"So, the &quot;real&quot; holiday is Saint Patrick's Feast Day, which is a day to honor Saint Patrick (the patron saint of Ireland) and how he drove out the snakes (pagans). Among the various standard traditions of Saint Feat Days (go to church, pray to them, appreciate what they got canonized for, etc), Saint Patrick's Day has a unique clause on it since it usually lands within the 6 weeks of Lent. On Saint Patrick's Day, the bans on eating and drinking during Lent are <i>lifted</i>, hence the propensity of massive quantities of alcohol to be consumed.<br /> <br /> Now, of course, in America (where the most Irish 99% of those claiming to be Irish get is to have an Irish ancestor from 150+ years ago) it's become about 2 things - pride in an Irish heritage and drinking a lot. As far as someone being gay being included or excluded.....well, that kinda goes hand-in-hand with it being a <i>Catholic </i>holiday first and an Irish one second. We all know where the usual official stance of the Catholic Church is about being gay.<br /> <br /> So, it's not just about being Irish, though that's most of it these days, especially here in 'Merikuh. Lan' uv duh Free an' home of Duh....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T07:01:24-07:00","id":93461,"title":"","content":"Ah ha. Thanks, Papa Bear.<br /> <br /> (I know I coulda just Googled that, but it's more fun to ask people.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T08:24:59-07:00","id":93501,"title":"","content":"I'm rather curious about how it got started in the US/North America specifically. Irish and Catholic pride are all well and good in the modern day, but it wasn't all that long ago that both these things were less welcome in the US than the plague.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T09:19:00-07:00","id":93521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=93501#post93501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm rather curious about how it got started in the US/North America specifically. Irish and Catholic pride are all well and good in the modern day, but it wasn't all that long ago that both these things were less welcome in the US than the plague.</div> </div> </div> </div>Irish people have often taken a deal of pride in elaborate ways to say &quot;fuck you&quot; to people who don't want them.<br /> <br /> As for what St. Patrick's Day is about... it's just another strategically placed festival day, same as Mardi Gras or Carnival. That it has anything more elaborate owes pretty much everything to the historical details of the Irish people.<br /> <br /> Catholic feast day or not, I don't think it's the Church organising any parades, soooo...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T10:25:52-07:00","id":93565,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Irish are uniquely gifted in giving the public the finger while raising the fist high in pride. Must be all the practice they got doing that to the English.<br /> <br /> And yeah, it's not the churches running the parades, it's the city. But they wouldn't be doing that if not for the pressure they got from the Irish-decent residents, most of whom are practicing or lapsed Catholics. One of the many back doors to the separation of church and state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T11:30:27-07:00","id":93618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solomon birch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=93399#post93399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not when done in fun. Unless little witches on Halloween are meant to represent Wiccans.</div> </div> </div> </div>ummm thats not how racism works. I can just about tolerate the whole 'rough and tumble irish domestic violence &amp; alcoholism are more socially acceptable from an irish person, that's to be expected' thing that's been doing the rounds for so long, but to have people throw a slur like 'mick' around is not my idea of a good time sorry","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T11:38:32-07:00","id":93629,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't really care for it.","sign