nt":"Then I'm honestly sorry to have hurt everybody's feelings. I didn't think it was that bad of a thing to say that I didn't want the dancing skeletons on all of the boards. The last thing I wanted was for people to feel as though I was lording anything over them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T17:51:36-07:00","id":209627,"title":"","content":"THAT, I didn't expect.<br /> <br /> Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T17:53:46-07:00","id":209630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=209604#post209604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: And really, Leaper? You think me telling you to &quot;leave off&quot; is a little abrasive when every time anyone sees your avatar they see a woman drinking a cup labeled <i>male tears</i>? Your idea of acceptable behavior is really quite different from mine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you explain your problem with this? I'm open to changing it, but it's always been a very tongue in cheek thing for me and I've gotten a lot of compliments for it in passing. It's supposed to be a joke at the expense of the 'Men's Rights' movement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T23:43:40-07:00","id":209871,"title":"","content":"My bed. It just caught me like I was Lois Lane and it was Superman.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T06:23:00-07:00","id":210068,"title":"","content":"Thank you for apologizing, Leaper. It was very much appreciated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=209630#post209630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you explain your problem with this? I'm open to changing it, but it's always been a very tongue in cheek thing for me and I've gotten a lot of compliments for it in passing. It's supposed to be a joke at the expense of the 'Men's Rights' movement.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, it exemplifies the problem with both the (radical) feminism and the men's rights movements. I believe in equality for all people. In that way, I am a feminist. The problem with &quot;feminism&quot; is that, in popular opinion, feminism has become a movement not to raise women up to the same level as men, but to put women on a higher plane and to stomp men down and crush them in a sort of revenge for the injustices done to women in the past. That is what I feel your avatar represents. Without context, it doesn't feel like a joke at the expense of the men's rights movement, but rather a jab at <i>all</i> men.<br /> <br /> In response to your earlier question, no, I don't really intend to keep in contact with these people. I only met them this last semester, so I have known them less than 13 weeks. And while I feel that there is a high level of potential for us to become very good friends if we continued to spend time together, we are not there. We're casual friends and I feel that it would be really awkward and seem clingy and needy to Skype together. I also don't really use Twitter. Furthermore, I have a, I don't know, mental glitch (?) where that kind of communication doesn't really work terribly effectively for me. An occasional Skype call seems artificial and forced. Casually seeing each other every so often, even if it's not randomly bumping into each other, seems more natural to me. I will text them occasionally, but that's probably the extent of my attempts.<br /> <br /> What I love: Yesterday, I was babysitting a 3 year old. We were at the park and he was playing on the playground equipment. While there, I saw a pair of children. One was a boy, whom I presume to be about 3-4. The other was a girl who was maybe 2-3 years his senior; I think she was his sister. The boy had some sort of mental or physical developmental problem; it was apparent from the look on his face and the way he acted and spoke. The little girl was helping him along. She would slide down the slide first, and then turn around and tell her brother to slide down. She would catch him at the bottom. Then she would walk with him up the stairs and make sure that the other kids weren't running across the bridge making it bounce while her brother crossed and repeat the process. The way she treated him was just so sweet for a girl that young. In a little way, it gave me hope for humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date: