 my bandage wet so i havent showered..it felt amazing. What i really want and love is steaming hot turn your skin red baths but my doc says not unless i wanna bleach the bathtub first x.x and i'm to lazy for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T13:37:17-07:00","id":212727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scelesta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=212720#post212720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ahhh I LOVE a steaming hot shower after being afraid for the last 6 days of getting my bandage wet so i havent showered..it felt amazing. What i really want and love is steaming hot turn your skin red baths but my doc says not unless i wanna bleach the bathtub first x.x and i'm to lazy for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Future tip from someone who's dealt with it: Shower when you're going to change the bandage/dressing. Remove the old, slap a water-tight seal over the wound (I usually use a plastic tape and a baggie, or just a large sealing bandage depending) and wash up. When you're done, peel the plastic seal off, clean the are with alcohol wipe and apply a fresh bandage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T13:48:48-07:00","id":212737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=212727#post212727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Future tip from someone who's dealt with it: Shower when you're going to change the bandage/dressing. Remove the old, slap a water-tight seal over the wound (I usually use a plastic tape and a baggie, or just a large sealing bandage depending) and wash up. When you're done, peel the plastic seal off, clean the are with alcohol wipe and apply a fresh bandage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh i just left the gauze on and showered figured it wouldnt hurt it to get warm water, cause my doc did say i could use warm compresses on it if it bothered me plust its been almost a week since it was cut open. I dunno if i could handle two rounds of tape pulling off in one session x.x My skin HATES adhesive tapes, in fact most make me itch and burn, the paper tape doesnt but it does stick so well it takes a few layers of skin off with it it which is fun o0 if it was on my arm i would care but inner thigh huuuurrttsss to pull tape off of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T22:26:21-07:00","id":213198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=212520#post212520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was fucked up. I like it. It genuinely creeped me out....and that ain't easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I found it creepy as well. I was &quot;grinning like a homicidal maniac&quot; whilst reading it, according to the friend that showed it to me. Ick is definitely my kind of creature. Creepy, yet indispensable.<br /> He's a genuinely harmful parasite, yet seemingly beholden to the one who feeds him and vice versa. He's the ultimate boogeyman in some ways, as unlike Slenderman or even the Ol' Closet Monster, he TELLS you that he loves you and continually PROVES it to you (in your mind, at least, it's all the proof you need. He did kill those monsters for you, after all. Come to think of it, weren't there less monsters before we had Ickbarr? Nah, couldn't be. Don't be silly. We NEED Ick.)<br /> He's your worst best friend. The most greedy of roommates. Ick reflects the continued dependence of the main character on their parents, and in general, on outside factors for safety. Ick kills the monsters. Ick makes the nightmares go away. He's all you need, after a while. You've stolen from your family to feed him. You've even killed a few dozen stray animals just to get Ick what he says he needs. Come to think of it....Was that man still breathing after we pried the last of his teeth from his head using alternating sides of a claw-hammer? No...the gurgling stopped after we finished with the premolars, remember? He just wouldn't stop screaming, but we had to feed Ickbarr, so down that hammer came until we could finish the job without a fuss.<br /> We'd do anything for Ick, to be honest. He's the only friend we have. I mean, who could we even relate to, after spending all that time loving a monster and relying on him to feel safe? No. All we need is Ickbarr. He's all we've ever needed. He says he loves me, and why would he lie? We love him too. More than anything else in the world.<br /> <br /> He's dependence. He's addiction. He's relying on others for shit you could do yourself, if you believed you could. He's the embodiment of self-doubt. That monster can be the most terrifying of all, and all you need to do is feed it to make it stronger, and you weaker. It will thank you with such gratitude when you feed it, but it justifies the suffering you've gone through by pointing out that You were ignoring It.<br /> He's my perfect boogeyman, because a tiny bit of him is in nearly everyone around me, in some way, especially myself. Make sure not to feed Ickbarr, kids. He's not good for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":".  I either edit my posts too much or not ENOUGH. Why will my words never be perfect??!?!? AAAAHHHHH!!! *rips off his own face* Ah. Okay. I feel better now. 07-30-2014, 09:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T16:52:34-07:00","id":214023,"title":"","content":"<i><a href=\"http://shirtoid.com/107599/kupocket/\" target=\"_blank\">ahhhh why did i never know this is a thing where is my credit card</a></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T07:11:01-07:00","id":215820,"title":"","content":"I got thye best sleep Ive had in months last night. It was drealess.