ider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T11:43:17-08:00","id":355916,"title":"","content":"I'm now officially a Wraith20 backer! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It was the first time I've had the opportunity to back a KS for a game, and it just feels good to know that I'm, in a tiny way, a part of something I love.<br /> <br /> &lt;3 WoD Forever","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T23:49:30-08:00","id":363240,"title":"","content":"Random human interaction that actually makes me happy.<br /> <br /> A good friend that I don't get the chance to converse with often has begun talking to me more. That in itself is good news, and something to be grateful for. I value my friends like the greatest of treasures. My family tolerates me. They sometimes even pretend to know me. <br /> My friends know me, and whether they give me shit or not, they accept me. I &quot;love&quot; my family, and would put my ass on the line for them, but it's my friends (if you're reading this, I might be talking about you) that I would trust to go into battle with. The ones I would rather spend my time with. Anyway, my friend has shown interest in letting me run a game night for him and some of my gaming buddies! I always respect anyone that lets me spend a few hours telling them an interactive story (unless they're assholes or stubbornly, purposefully ignorant, then fuck em), but it actually made me genuinely smile and get a little spring in my step, knowing that my friend wants to game with me. Granted, a few of my other players are definitely excited about a new player to save the universe with, but it's a special happiness for me.<br /> <br /> Someone actually went &quot;Huh. I wonder what Az is up to. Oh, cool, he's running a game! I wanna play!&quot;. It's a small thing, but it mattered a lot. It nearly broke my damn face. I had almost forgotten what a grin felt like.<br /> <br /> Fuck.<br /> <br /> I have hope for happiness and a future and everything now. Stupid domino effect making me rethink existence and find a reason to live. <br /> <br /> Heh. Of all the things I've lost, I miss my mind the most.<br /> <br /> Doorknob, always eating all the fries and blaming me. I was busy smoking!<br /> <br /> \u200b<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signa