nyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T10:00:17-08:00","id":416585,"title":"","content":"I don't like talking abortion with close-minded religion freaks, but I did enjoy this little bit from last night.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Douchebag</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Sean, what is a gospel matter for one is a gospel matter for all w whether they believe our not. The rest of your diatribe fell flat on that premise.</b></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><br /> <br /> </span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcane</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Well, no, it doesn't. It just shows you have no respect for people who don't believe the same things as you, which makes you a terrible missionary, which...Well, quite frankly I don't think I need to explain the importance of that to you.<br /> <br /> Also, it dis</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">plays a narrowness of thought in two ways. 1)It shows that without your religion, you have no real knowledge or deliberation of the subject. No one has any reason to take you seriously outside of the church, and inside the church all you have is circle-jerking each other due to belief. 2) A failure to even bother considering what I said after the fact shows that you have no desire to even consider another person's perspective. You don't want dialogue, you want confirmation, and no one's going to give that to you in the real world, and a continued insistence on this will make you a bitter man who poisons everyone around you with your close-mindedness. In short, you will become a magnificent Pharisee. Good Job.<br /> <br /> The first priority of God is to bring people into the fold. If you adopt an attitude that excludes any thought other than your own, you become a closed gate for the Holy Spirit, utterly useless to your Father.<br /> <br /> On top of that, if we all turn out to be wrong, you'll look quite the douchebag, but that's neither here nor there.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Douchebag</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You make quite the missionary telling people what they want to hear. Your language is also not quite pleasing for a priesthood holder.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Douchebag</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">When you build your house upon the sand by basing your arguments and missionary work on a falsehood, it will all get washed away with the rain.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><br /> <br /> </span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcane</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">1) If you read what I said, you'll notice I didn't say at the end to tell them what they want to hear. I said let's not treat a serious discussion like it's binary discussion. It pays to understand how others think about it, to sympathize with the posi</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">tion, and acknowledge the concerns in order to help communicate answers one believes to be true. We aren't lighthouses who can just shine gospel light on people and convince them of what we believe-we're bridges, and the roads that lead to Christ are made from what we believe mixed in with empathy and understanding for the other side. We don't shove with our hands, we extend them for people to take. If that doesn't sound Christ-like to you, that's your problem.<br /> <br /> 2)Anything to ignore something inconvenient, eh (Douchebag). Consider this: If you don't care about actually caring about other people and their perspective, than why the flying fuck should I care about my language around you? <b>Are you asking that I understand and respect your position and beliefs, even as I share my beliefs with you? </b>Cause that's a lovely double standard we're both practicing.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T15:27:14-08:00","id":418032,"title":"","content":"My friends.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Last game I had a lasombra, played by the st, try to kill me so I blew up my own haven with 180kg of c4. Almost the whole cotorie was in there. 2 of 9 players survived. But they were all plotting with the lasombra </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T16:17:48-08:00","id":418064,"title":"","c