s entire post possible.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T04:56:01-07:00","id":584521,"title":"","content":"That's... a bit too much Joey. 8+ grams? When you get back to this plane of consciouness please PM or post here to know you are alright.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T19:39:30-07:00","id":585540,"title":"","content":"It was somewhere between 8 and 9.5 grams.<br /> <br /> It was the longest and most psychologically jarring trip of my life.<br /> <br /> I'm alright now, but things were iffy for awhile. Thanks for the concern, Thorbesy. =) it's appreciated. *bro hug*<br /> <br /> Ok, I'll dispense with the dramatics. I took the things for medicinal purposes, believe it or not. There's a lot of anecdotal evidence that psilocybin can help with depression, sometimes for weeks or months after a trip. I've experienced the phenomenon before, in my late teens. I realize it sounds a bit extreme, but I've tried dozens of mood stabilizers and antidepressants over the years and nothing else has ever had an appreciable and helpful effect. I was desperate.<br /> <br /> So far, things are feeling better. I'm not experiencing the extreme moodswings that usually pepper my day. I'm not contemplating the sadness of existence. I'm just here. Being a person. It's very unusual for me. I like it.<br /> <br /> About the actual trip, for the curious:<br /> <br /> It started with music becoming AMAZING. Music was existence.<br /> During a Hard House mix, I might have not had a physical body.<br /> <br /> Then things got spooky. I suddenly forgot that the rest of my house existed, and for most of the trip labored under the delusion that my bedroom and bathroom were actually a seaside cottage of some sort, Jaws meets Ernest Hemingway.<br /> <br /> I lost chunks of time, but remember that I failed miserably at eating an apple.<br /> Afterwards, that apple was a weird piece of modern art for me.<br /> <br /> Then I alternately hugged my pillow and sat in front of my fan, depending on how uncomfortable I was.<br /> <br /> I quoted Lethal Weapon numerous times during my more lucid moments, because I'm apparently too old for this shit. <br /> <br /> At some point, I remember being convinced that literally EVERYTHING was sharks. If you don't know what that means...me either.<br /> <br /> After that, things started evening out.<br /> <br /> \u200bI won't be doing THAT again for a long time. Possibly never.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 07-09-2015, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T01:07:24-07:00","id":585749,"title":"","content":"Thanks brother.<br /> <br /> I'm glad to know you are feeling so well in the after-trip, hope it last. Still think you might have overdosed but as everything seems to be fine and dandy I won't complain anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T09:27:09-07:00","id":586206,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/65219-your-headcanon?p=552531#post552531\">Finding someone liked a post you wrote long after you wrote it.</a><br /> <br /> &quot;-Huh-wha? Somebody actually liked that? I barely even remember writing that! Well... yay me, I guess.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","