v> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T21:42:11-07:00","id":647661,"title":"","content":"I like this idea I am having for a Classic WoD fanfiction. It's based on old nostalgic memories of the chronicles I'd play and run with my younger brothers and occasionally one or two friends from school when I was 12-13 years old. We mostly played D&amp;D 3.5 (a heavily house ruled and homebrewed variant of it, anyway) but we also played Vampire The Masquerade using only the 2e corebook and little else. Then I moved to Roanoke and we discovered Big Eyes Small Mouth and New World of Darkness, as well as the rest of the Classic WoD as well.<br /> <br /> Well, the idea is that it's a story within a story, using fictionalized versions of my younger self, my brothers, and my friends (names will be changed of course). Things won't be exactly the same as the old games as it's been literally a decade since those days, and I'll be focusing on the actual campaign's story more than the framing story. I kind of like this idea I am having and I look forward to writing this fanfic and posting it over on the Masquerade forum if the mods are okay with fanfiction being posted here. I hope you guys will like the story once it starts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":""