e haha</div> </div> </div> </div>It's stuff like this that shows me we'll be friends forever. xD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T13:16:51-07:00","id":649249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=647661#post647661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this idea I am having for a Classic WoD fanfiction. It's based on old nostalgic memories of the chronicles I'd play and run with my younger brothers and occasionally one or two friends from school when I was 12-13 years old. We mostly played D&amp;D 3.5 (a heavily house ruled and homebrewed variant of it, anyway) but we also played Vampire The Masquerade using only the 2e corebook and little else. Then I moved to Roanoke and we discovered Big Eyes Small Mouth and New World of Darkness, as well as the rest of the Classic WoD as well.<br /> <br /> Well, the idea is that it's a story within a story, using fictionalized versions of my younger self, my brothers, and my friends (names will be changed of course). Things won't be exactly the same as the old games as it's been literally a decade since those days, and I'll be focusing on the actual campaign's story more than the framing story. I kind of like this idea I am having and I look forward to writing this fanfic and posting it over on the Masquerade forum if the mods are okay with fanfiction being posted here. I hope you guys will like the story once it starts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It sounds quite interesting. I look forward to reading! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T11:27:26-07:00","id":654105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://youtu.be/Scu81EW4UC8\" data-code=\"Scu81EW4UC8\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Scu81EW4UC8/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> *does the Truffle Shuffle for y'all*<br /> <br /> You know I love you, right? You're always good enough for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T05:20:11-07:00","id":660606,"title":"","content":"Woke up feeling pretty good today. I have a light day of work (just two patients), I'll swing by the auctioneer to pre-sign the contracts for selling my place (which is almost at market value now) and my dad's place (which is...not, but still, auctions don't matter until the final day), I'll drop off an application for a duplex I really want, and...one more thing.<br /> <br /> Yesterday I was texting with a friend about the assholes outside Planned Parenthood. &quot;Look at those assholes,&quot; we sneered, &quot;with their signs that try to encapsulate a very complex issue in a three-word slogan. Boy, we sure are smarter than those assholes!&quot; But after, oh, I want to say the third text on the topic, I started to feel pretty guilty about having said that. I mean, yes, anyone who thinks a bumper sticker can accurately encapsulate the complexity of the abortion issue is an asshole, but how would I know that's what the protestors actually think? I've never spoken to them, never asked them, never given them a chance. I just drive by them at 35 MPH, reading signs intended to be read by an audience passing by at 35 MPH, and congratulate myself on being so much smarter and deeper than people whose philosophies I genuinely don't know.<br /> <br /> I didn't correct that error yesterday because I was wearing scrubs with the company logo on them. It's a bad idea to get in an abortion argument in the street while wearing your company's colors. Today, though, I'm going to bring a jacket along to cover myself up decently and ask the protestors if they're part of a formal group and what services their group offers to support the women they're picketing against. I owe that to myself if not to them, so I can at least be honest.<br /> <br /> I really, really hate confrontation, though (it embarrasses me), so I'm glad I woke up feeling good. I'll need this energy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T08:20:26-07:00","id":660724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=660606#post660606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really, really hate confrontation, though (it embarrasses me), so I'm glad I woke up feeling good. I'll need this energy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me know what the results of the inquires are. I am curious as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T16:11:38-07:00","id":661213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=660724#post660724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me know what the results of the inquires are. I am curious as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't happen today. I forgot my goddamned jacket. Don't worry, though, I just threw it into my passenger's seat so I won't be able to forget it Monday.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T14:54:52-07:00","id":662239,"title":"","content":"Two things to love today:<br /> <br /> First, that even though I've been absent this forum for quite some time there are still familiar names here posting. Hello again, everyone.<br /> <br /> Second, and even more to love, I'm finally on medication that I can afford and that works without incapacitating side effects, so I no longer live life in constant physical pain and nearly soul-crushing depression - and on top of that in the last few weeks since starting this medication I've already lost 15 of the 150 pounds I hope to lose.<br /> <br /> I'm feeling great for the first time in years, and I thought it'd be nice to share that with some old cyber-friends.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T03:15:16-07:00","id":662862,"title":"","content":"I'm so glad for you, Drake. Hope the good streak continues on forever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T19:29:56-07:00","id":663762,"title":"","content":"Forever? Just hope it lasts a long time, man. Don't lock him down with your magical powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T11:21:44-07:00","id":665922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=660724#post660724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me know what the results of the inquires are. I am curious as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't been able to find any protestors lately. I'm going to guess it's because of <a href=\"http://lakeexpo.com/news/lake_news/planned-parenthood-investigation-in-missouri-widens-to-dhhs-public-universities/article_f213a708-5810-11e5-9b59-ab4be9ed265f.html\" target=\"_blank\">this folderol;</a> that the pro-life advocates are busy attending or appearing outside of hearings.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to forget my resolve on this. I need this. I need to know, and I need to demonstrate enough spine to have the conversation. I will keep looking...but be patient with me. The protestors gotta meet me halfway on this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T03:08:11-07:00","id":666663,"title":"","content":"I realized something:<br /> <br /> I'd forgotten who the FUCK I AM. I am Azrael the motherfucking Firestorm, Archangel of Death appointed by no God but Baphomet.<br /> <br /> I'm Nightbreed. Joey is the skin I wear to hang out with the Naturals and hunt for decent meat. I felt such needless guilt. Like a cross I nailed myself to just to prove I would. I'm quite the show off. In the end, mothered by a She-wolf, fathered by a clown. Taught the art of taking someone apart in combat by my own masked man, and my own desire for power.<br /> <br /> I'm a beast. Do you like beasts? It really doesn't matter to me, but maybe you'll smile. Smiling is fun.<br /> <br /> My favorite part of smiling is when people think you're doing it, but really, you're just baring your teeth at them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If you're my friend and this answers some questions, I'm glad.<br /> If you're not, and you feel worried by this: worry about your mortality. It's running, running, running out. And you quiver in your human skin. If you get too scared because the night is dark, I'm happy to take your meat. Wouldn't want you to live in fear, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T19:28:30-07:00","id":675953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=660724#post660724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me know what the results of the inquires are. I am curious as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I finally got the chance today.<br /> <br /> Let's get this out of the way: The protesters outside the Planned Parenthood in my town do offer services to refer women to alternate medical and counseling resources to support them in the choice to keep their pregnancies. I cannot, at this time, testify as to the quality of those services, but my biggest concern--that the protesters want to restrict women's choices while accepting no responsibility for ensuring the only choice left is a useful and productive one--is at least partially answered. They do offer services to women. <u>Whatever other complaints I have against the position or their methodologies, the protesters take steps to support women.</u><br /> <br /> That said, my cynicism is really blaring on this one. The group protesting is one called 40 Days for Life, which the spokesperson (by which I mean one of the two retired women walking around outside) seems to base its entire premise on religious grounds. According to the literature I received, their entire plan is to pray and fast for forty days, at which point God will...hang on, let me quote the pamphlet...&quot;heal our land.&quot; Heal it of abortion, presumably. This is a really sore issue for me for reasons I won't go into fully because I don't want my anger to seem like I'm directing it at our Christian friends here on the boards,* so I'll just say it does not sit well with my beliefs that they would rather pray than, I don't know, contact their state and federal representatives. I'm not Christian, but I was raised Christian, and I was taught that grace and healing are gifts God gives, not objectives that can be purchased at the price of prayer. It feels insupportably arrogant to me to think that I can hand God a voucher for X amount of people praying Y hard for Z period of time and haggling that into a payment God is obligated to accept and repay.<br /> <br /> Despite the protesters' complete focus on religion, though, I did my best to find out what they actually do for the women and the children they target, and I must admit their position seemed rooted in compassion to me. They mentioned the tragedy of abortion a lot, which, fine, yeah, I gotta give them that. Every woman who's ever told me about her abortion has described feeling guilt and regret for years afterward, so wanting to spare women that is a pretty noble cause.<br /> <br /> I just wish I didn't get such an air of sales pitch about it, you know? The constant repetition of religious beliefs and invitations to pray seemed like clumsy attempts to indoctrinate me, and I couldn't help noticing the protesters did not ever once ask me a question about my beliefs, because they didn't care what my beliefs were except to train them to match their beliefs. It's a bummer, but fine, whatever, I guess I can't really fault people who seem abortion as murder for not asking me what my stance on murdering babies is. You probably start from the assumption that no one likes killing babies.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the story is pretty anticlimactic, since most of it was about religion and I don't care to hear that as the basis for legal arguments. The protesters have more actual procedures in place than I expected, but fewer than I'd hope (seriously, &quot;ask God to make it all better&quot; is just not a political ideology I can get behind, whether I agree with the issue at hand or not). So while I remain opposed to their goals, I do feel that fairness requires me give them more credit than I did in the day.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Hi, Arc and Jeddy. Miss you guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":271,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","user":"JimB","date":". 09-23-2015, 10:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T21:12:20-07:00","id":675997,"title":"","content":"We're still here, and you should know we're not exactly thin-skinned people. I won't speak for Br(though I think he and I are in accordance), but there's also the fact that I am very, very, <i>very </i>pro-choice, and very much in line with &quot;Get off your ass and <i>do</i> something&quot; when it comes to....well, anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T21:21:57-07:00","id":676000,"title":"","content":"I love seeing people trying to better themselves through knowledge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">They call me... Mr. Demmywinks.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1210-demetrius7997","name":"Demetrius7997","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T21:22:46-07:00","id":676001,"title":"","content":"You inspired/motivated me to go look up some information...<br /> <br /> From their website:<br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Sentinel SSm A\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">A fast is not a Christian diet; it is a powerful means of drawing closer to God by blocking out distractions. Fast from certain foods. Fast from television. Fast from apathy and indifference. Fast from whatever it is that separates you from God.</span></span></span>&quot;<br /> <br /> So when they say &quot;fast&quot; they don't mean what most people mean by fast.<br /> <br /> Additionally on the website they have no links or actual published connections to support groups... which make sense since the whole thing is based around an extended flash mob effect. the idea being that everyone comes together to protest/pray/raise awareness for 40 days, and then goes away until next year.<br /> <br /> And of course it's hugely successful! Because God has heard the prayers, thus every abortion clinic closure, every employee that quits or is fired is of course God's work and they claim credit for such progress towards their cause.<br /> <br /> The website does however contain strong advertisements for the book the leaders of the group have written, amazingly also called 40 days. Looking up the book on amazon it's an amazing all 5-star review, every single review, all singing the praises of the book. Now I'm not saying that they encouraged members of the organization to pump up it's rating with praise and thus sales, but it's remarkably similar in style.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now I'm old and cynical... well... I'm getting old and have always been cynical. But this particular organization raises the odor of a group that wants to raise awareness and support of the group first, channel some righteous indignation into a cause second, and help people third. I mean this are people that are counting the pope as a supporter because they got a standard &quot;yes if you're opposing abortion you are right&quot; message from the vatican at one point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T21:30:42-07:00","id":676013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=675997#post675997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're still here, and you should know we're not exactly thin-skinned people. I won't speak for Br(though I think he and I are in accordance), but there's also the fact that I am very, very, <i>very </i>pro-choice, and very much in line with &quot;Get off your ass and <i>do</i> something&quot; when it comes to....well, anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>At this risk of spawning a political debate, I dislike framing it purely as a binary argument.<br /> <br /> My own view is that abortion is a sad and terrible thing, and I would like the world to move towards a place where non-medical-reason abortions don't happen. Effectively anti-abortion. However, the way to do that (IMO) isn't banning abortions, we've seen far too much of what that results in... improper facilities, women trying to induce abortion through violence or chemical abuse, and in the more &quot;polite&quot; society deliberate misdiagnosis in medical facilities. Education, free and easily accessible birth control for all women, improved research into male birth control, and free and easily accessible birth control for men. Reduce abortions by dramatically cutting back on the unintentional pregnancies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T04:50:37-07:00","id":676307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=676001#post676001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So when they say &quot;fast&quot; they don't mean what most people mean by fast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, they mean it as a focus for the ritual casting of a spell that will draw down God.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=676001#post676001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally on the website they have no links or actual published connections to support groups...</div> </div> </div> </div>I can sort of defend that with a clear conscience: The protesters here in town have printed information they hand out to anyone who asks, as well as to anyone who tries to cross over the trespass line, whether coming or going. It has a list of local facilities and services a person can use. So while I can't speak for the international organization, the protesters I personally have experience of are trying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=676001#post676001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...which make sense since the whole thing is based around an extended flash mob effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is maybe the best way to put it.<br /> <br /> The rest of what you said...yeah, I can't really defend the group. I can only speak to my experience with the two individuals I met, and they were better than I would have guessed from their protest signs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":271,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","user":"JimB","date":". 09-24-2015, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T05:29:03-07:00","id":676322,"title":"","content":"I remember in middle school some activists hung out outside the fence by the field for a few days, luring kids over and giving them little comics with drawn depictions of abortions of happy cartoon babies.<br /> <br /> I was almost aborted myself, it probably would have been a lot easier on my birth mother and a lot less of a painful reminder, instead she gave me away.<br /> <br /> But I'm pro-choice. And while I'm in agreement with Odd_Canuck about trying to educate people and let them know it isn't a binary option, I'm not anti-abortion. I think the foster and adoption system could use a lot of work but it's important work and the kind of thing that needs to be improved.<br /> <br /> Odd topic for 'You know what I love.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-24-2015, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T06:30:31-07:00","id":676345,"title":"","content":"I love that this is a civil discussion on abortion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T07:27:10-07:00","id":676368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=676013#post676013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At this risk of spawning a political debate, I dislike framing it purely as a binary argument.<br /> <br /> My own view is that abortion is a sad and terrible thing, and I would like the world to move towards a place where non-medical-reason abortions don't happen. Effectively anti-abortion. However, the way to do that (IMO) isn't banning abortions, we've seen far too much of what that results in... improper facilities, women trying to induce abortion through violence or chemical abuse, and in the more &quot;polite&quot; society deliberate misdiagnosis in medical facilities. Education, free and easily accessible birth control for all women, improved research into male birth control, and free and easily accessible birth control for men. Reduce abortions by dramatically cutting back on the unintentional pregnancies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Completely fair.<br /> <br /> Trying to speak quickly on things is never as effective as you'd think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-24-2015, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","av