s://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T10:29:31-07:00","id":1102555,"title":"","content":"Loved seeing a perspective from a current Onyx Path/White Wolf writer I previously disliked, totally alter my opinion about him with a few sentences. It was about something I feel very strongly about, so seeing this totally made my day. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T15:34:30-07:00","id":1102627,"title":"","content":"Life Is Strange prequel being officially announced. I expected a sequel in a different setting, which will happen, but not a prequel in addition to that.<br /> <br /> Cannot understate how the first one was a really, really, REALLY big deal for me, so there's that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T15:47:49-07:00","id":1102635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=1102627#post1102627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Life Is Strange prequel being officially announced. I expected a sequel in a different setting, which will happen, but not a prequel in addition to that.<br /> <br /> Cannot understate how the first one was a really, really, REALLY big deal for me, so there's that</div> </div> </div> </div>Not familiar with the game, though it's free on PS Plus. How was it a big deal for you, if it's not invading privacy to ask?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T16:15:10-07:00","id":1102639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=1102635#post1102635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not familiar with the game, though it's free on PS Plus. How was it a big deal for you, if it's not invading privacy to ask?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not, no worries. The short version is that I do love little town settings were things are darker than they seem (think Stephen King's works, Twin Peaks or Gravity Falls) and while looking for inspiration for writing a CoD one, I found Life Is Strange (which cites King and Lynch as its main inspiration, making things go full circle).<br /> <br /> It's not exactly horror, more a fiction strictly focused on characters that use time travel as a narrative device, but I loved its atmosphere, protagonists and pace. I don't want to spoil it in case you decide to pick it up, but it involves a lot of the classic time travel tropes in an unusual setting, telling a story that has a lot of heart and emotion. It's not perfect by a long shot and with some knowledge of its tropes and inspirations you are able to spot some twists, but has a lot to give to those who are willing to give it a chance.<br /> <br /> Can't exactly say why but I found myself absorbed by it and after the game was done I looked for some discussions with other fans. I found groups of people who shared my thoughts and made several good new friends out of it, which it's something that's not always easy for me for a long list of reasons. Even got into a relationship thanks to it and, though it eventually ended, the whole experience gave me the chance to know people and be appreciated just because I wanted to talk about something I loved.<br /> <br /> It was nice, taught me some lessons and even gave me the motivation to be a bit more daring when it comes to talking about things you're passionate about, which is also one of the reasons I'm trying to be more active around here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T16:20:30-07:00","id":1103319,"title":"","content":"I love coming up with ideas for fanfiction and starting to write up the rough drafts. Currently working on some World of Darkness fics, both Classic and New.<br /> <br /> In particular, I had some ideas for fics inspired by the first edition of Vampire: The Requiem but with some modifications. Once I get some material posted, I'll link them to you guys to check out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts