-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=1245012#post1245012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, a short article about John Carpenter I finished to write today is getting published in a small magazine and I'm even getting paid for it. Not much, but enough to buy another book or a something like that.<br /> <br /> Little things, but enough to call this a good day.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think getting published should ever count as a little thing. That's awesome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T06:57:30-07:00","id":1245863,"title":"","content":"I love homemade sweet tea. Just brewed a whole gallon of it a few minutes ago and I'm waiting for it to cool down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T22:52:01-07:00","id":1248329,"title":"","content":"I love when someone helps cut down on the complexity of an idea, but doesn't cut down the enthusiasm that went into it and in fact inspires more for doing so. It's a tricky thing to do, but when it's done it's just golden. Recently had that happen with me and a Changeling idea I had.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-26T18:45:47-07:00","id":1249044,"title":"","content":"I just discovered that folklorists and modern anthropologist are not fond of Joseph Campbell's work and I'm so glad that's a thing because now I feel I'm allowed to not care much for what the man wrote and basically ignore him as I almost always prefer to do. Or at the very least aknowledge his stuff only to subvert the points I despise the most.<br /> <br /> The forum's still having some issues for me, but that was such a pleasant discovery I can live with this being the only post I manage to make for the next few days. <br /> <br /> (Just a few though, because I realized I lose a rather important portion of my social activities without this place. I got used to all of you cool people)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-26T18:58:13-07:00","id":1249045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=1249044#post1249044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just discovered that folklorists and modern anthropologist are not fond of Joseph Campbell's work and I'm so glad that's a thing because now I feel I'm allowed to not care much for what the man wrote and basically ignore him as I almost always prefer to do. Or at the very least aknowledge his stuff only to subvert the points I despise the most.<br /> <br /> The forum's still having some issues for me, but that was such a pleasant discovery I can live with this being the only post I manage to make for the next few days.<br /> <br /> (Just a few though, because I realized I lose a rather important portion of my social activities without this place. I got used to all of you cool people)</div> </div> </div> </div>He's really such a joke, academically speaking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-26T19:02:25-07:00","id":1249046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=1249045#post1249045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's really such a joke, academically speaking.</div> </div> </div> </div>My anthropology professor loved him, I had to endure more than I could digest about Campbell, and thus I thought that that was the norm. I'm glad I was wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 08-26-2018, 10:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T04:50:38-07:00","id":1249095,"title":"","content":"Campbell is no &quot;God&quot;, but he wrote some significant stuff, &quot;Who Goes There?&quot; which is the basis for The Thing From Another World and John Carpenter's The Thing are a must for any horror fan, tho I wouldn't assume every horror fan holds him in their top ten or something<br /> <br /> I wouldn't go saying anyone should read all his works, but if you're gonna read from the golden age of science fiction, read Who Goes There, if you want to see one of the most highly regarded horror movies, watch JC's The Thing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24473-willowfang","name":"Willowfang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T05:05:54-07:00","id":1249096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Willowfang</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=1249095#post1249095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Campbell is no &quot;God&quot;, but he wrote some significant stuff, &quot;Who Goes There?&quot; which is the basis for The Thing From Another World and John Carpenter's The Thing are a must for any horror fan, tho I wouldn't assume every horror fan holds him in their top ten or something<br /> <br /> I wouldn't go saying anyone should read all his works, but if you're gonna read from the golden age of science fiction, read Who Goes There, if you want to see one of the most highly regarded horror movies, watch JC's The Thing</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm speaking of Joseph Campbell, the author of The Hero with a Thousand Faces, not the John W. Campbell of <i>Astounding Science Fiction </i>fame you're mentioning.<br /> <br /> (Though John W. Campbell was not a saint regarding certain topics, let's be fair. But having some of the authors of that era having truly despicable opinions on certain matters is nothing new)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 08-27-2018, 08:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T05:12:48-07:00","id":1249097,"title":"","content":"Ah, kk, yeah, seems like he was a provocateur on slavery at least. But hard to say if some people from the past were just products of their time, (sad enough) or truely reprehensible on certain subjects","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24473-willowfang","name":"Willowfang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T06:18:32-07:00","id":1249106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Willowfang</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=1249097#post1249097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, kk, yeah, seems like he was a provocateur on slavery at least. But hard to say if some people from the past were just products of their time, (sad enough) or truely reprehensible on certain subjects</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a topic I have to confront with more often than I'd like to, because several authors I love also happen to have awful personal views. Generally, I think that &quot;product of their time&quot; does not cut it for me.<br /> <br /> I'm on the Guillermo Del Toro's side of the debate: love the works for what they gave to you and appreciate what they added to the common imaginery, but also confront with the authors you respect and always remember their faults no matter what. Then, aim to make things better.<br /> <br /> It's not the only way to deal with the issue, but it's the one that works for me. Overall, lots of great books, movies and comics happened because fans decided to process their feelings towards problematic authors of the past, so things could be worse.<br /> <br /> Then again, I'm a huge Lovecraft fan even if the man insulted my ethnicity several times. I'm pretty much forced to have an opinion on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T04:29:45-07:00","id":1249665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=1249106#post1249106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then again, I'm a huge Lovecraft fan even if the man insulted my ethnicity several times. I'm pretty much forced to have an opinion on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, Lovecraft gets a worse rap than he deserves. The guy started out with opinions fairly average for his time and progressed as he matured. A lot of the reason why Lovecraft comes off as <i> double plus</i> <i>ultra</i> racist is that people he corresponded with tended to be on the cutting edge of social progress, making him look a neanderthal by comparison. And because many of his works are open to shallow racist readings, like taking Shadow Over Innsmouth as a screed against miscegenation rather than biological determinism - an issue Lovecraft was struggling with at the time.<br /> <br /> What I'm trying to say is that yes, Lovecraft <i>was</i> racist, but he wasn't this Jim Crow-esque pillar of xenophobia modern pop culture likes to paint him as.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T06:32:58-07:00","id":1249686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=1249665#post1249665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, Lovecraft gets a worse rap than he deserves. The guy started out with opinions fairly average for his time and progressed as he matured. A lot of the reason why Lovecraft comes off as <i> double plus</i> <i>ultra</i> racist is that people he corresponded with tended to be on the cutting edge of social progress, making him look a neanderthal by comparison. And because many of his works are open to shallow racist readings, like taking Shadow Over Innsmouth as a screed against miscegenation rather than biological determinism - an issue Lovecraft was struggling with at the time.<br /> <br /> What I'm trying to say is that yes, Lovecraft <i>was</i> racist, but he wasn't this Jim Crow-esque pillar of xenophobia modern pop culture likes to paint him as.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trust me, you don't need to explain that to me. My &quot;I'm a huge Lovecraft fan&quot; is less &quot;I read his books and like them&quot; and more &quot;I read his books, his letters, what his peers wrote about him, what his peers wrote in general, essays of all sorts about him, the S.T. Joshi's biography and my college thesis is about him&quot;. I don't bring <i>that</i> up when speaking casually about him, because, honestly, I'm a nobody and who cares, but Lovecraft is pretty much the only thing out there I'm really confident about.<br /> <br /> Since I brought Lovecraft up in the first place though: I agree his racism is not a core element of his works as such as pop culture paints it to be, I agree that there's more to him than that and that his contributions to literature and modern culture are huge and owe little to racism (except <i>Horror at Red Hook, </i>but screw that story) and it irritates me that's almost impossible to discuss Lovecraft without having to consider the topic when <i>many</i> other famous authors were just as bad and seemingly immune to this.<br /> <br /> But Lovecraft was a pillar of xenophobia. Not of the Jim Crow-esque kind, but of his own, more intellectual and reclusive kind. I mean, it's hard to deny. It does not feel good when you have to face it personally. And I got it easy! I can't blame Samuel Loveman for having repudiated Lovecraft after he discovered how anti-semite he was.<br /> <br /> The thing with Lovecraft is that his racism is <i>weird</i>. He was, and that's the exact term I always wanted to use when I discussed him academically, a fucking dork. He was a man with issues that grew up mostly alone and built his personal perspective on impersonal absurdities. The kind of fucking dork that as a teen writes (paraphrased) &quot;I am ashamed that the colonies gained the independence when we could still be part of the glorious British Empire&quot; when his family is proud to having had a role in the US independence and that consequently hurts their reputation.<br /> <br /> Several of his most problematic personal views developed in this little, isolated bubble, and Lovecraft could not reconcile them with reality when the occasion called for it. He was also stubborn as a mule, which does not help. In turn, this lead to these awkward situations where Lovecraft was perhaps not a practical racist but remained a fiercely intellectual one.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Sure, I married Sonia Greene, a Jewish woman, but now that she's my wife that's part of her past&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Sure, I'll hang with Samuel Loveman, he's Jewish but he's a good one, unlike those I don't know&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Sure, I'll become the mentor of the young Robert Bloch. He's Jewish too, you say? Who cares, Robert's great. He killed me in one of his stories. Hilarious&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Sure, Zelia Bishop is a fine young woman. I enjoy our interactions and she's a brilliant mind. So glad some young ladies manage to enlighten themselves like that&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Sure, now that Robert Howard mentions it, perhaps I might consider that not all the african-american people are that bad. But only some&quot; </i>(Speaking for the times, at least. Bob Howard did his best)<br /> <br /> That sort of stuff. Lovecraft always had trouble reconciling his lifelong convinctions with what happened in the actual world. He wrote both &quot;I know he's a clown, but by God, I like the boy&quot; when talking about Hitler (which is a tough one to forget) and &quot;I distrust fascism. One can't tolerate much a system whose followers declare &quot;Enemy of Mankind&quot; whoever disagrees with it&quot;.<br /> <br /> I think the thing is that Lovecraft's bizarre racism was more a symptom of the issues and inner conflicts the man. Lovecraft felt out of place, out of time and thought to belong to a mankind that was not there. He saw the cosmic horror because he lived it. Which is actually the real source of its best works and the actual origin of his greatness, I think. <br /> <br /> I can go on for hours but I think that proved my point. Things with Lovecraft aren't easy. Some say &quot;I liked Lovecraft because he hated (terrible epithets)&quot; (no really, I know several who said this) and others say &quot;I hate Lovecraft because he's the absolute incarnation of white, American racism&quot;. Neither is right, but racism was a rather big, cumbersome element of ol' H.P. personality. Not as important as many people think, but it's hard to blame them for it. They have all the reasons to dismiss him when the racism thing arises.<br /> <br /> Some did not. Neil Gaiman, Stephen King, Alan Moore, Thomas Ligotti, Mike Mignola, Guillermo Del Toro...the list goes on. More recently, awesome stuff like <i>Lovecraft Country </i>and <i>Get Out </i>happened when Lovecraft fans decided to confront with the man's racism. As for me, I just wrote terrible lovecraftian pastiches that nobody should ever read.<br /> <br /> But I owe to Lovecraft a lot. When I was just a kid and some teacher picked on me through all the middle school, turning a boy who loved to read and into an emotional wreck that could not bear to open a book and hated both himself and all things school related, it was Lovecraft that brought me back from the edge. So I am rather biased. Guess I love that, just to say this is on topic?<br /> <br /> And we got here from a bit of confusion between Joseph and John Campbell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 01-22-2020, 09:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T12:56:16-07:00","id":1249754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=1249686#post1249686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing with Lovecraft is that his racism is <i>weird</i>. He was, and that's the exact term I always wanted to use when I discussed him academically, a fucking dork. He was a man with issues that grew up mostly alone and built his personal perspective on impersonal absurdities. The kind of fucking dork that as a teen writes (paraphrased) &quot;I am ashamed that the colonies gained the independence when we could still be part of the glorious British Empire&quot; when his family is proud to having had a role in the US independence and that consequently hurts their reputation</div> </div> </div> </div>...Guldurnit, H.P. Lovecraft was a turn of the century equivalent to a modern otaku weeaboo who makes great memes. That... makes almost too <i>much</i> sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 08-29-2018, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T12:27:03-07:00","id":1250029,"title":"","content":"Sometimes people can be so kind without prompting, just naturally expressi