 Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T12:09:11-07:00","id":1257002,"title":"","content":"I love that my toddler decided to name his stuffed dragon toy &quot;Happy.&quot; Not even a mistake like I thought that's what he wanted. He used the hand sign for it and everything. So I've got a stuffed dragon in my living room and its name is Happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24219-goddessgood","name":"goddessgood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-04T20:27:28-07:00","id":1258995,"title":"","content":"Update from my earlier Hate post:<br /> <br /> I got every childish thing I whined for!*<br /> <br /> Today was, all told, a good one. I feel loved. I ate like a five year old. I watched cartoons with my soulmate while sipping cocoa. My back doesn't feel like it's mutating into a pullout couch. Things worked out better than expected, and I'm grateful for every bit of that.<br /> <br /> Score one for optimism.<br /> <br /> *I couldn't wear the TMNT pajamas. Apparently, I've grown since then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-16T14:20:42-07:00","id":1261001,"title":"","content":"I was already sold on They From Beneath The Sea! but, after the latest preview, I can say I have the money for the Kickstarter here, waiting to get spent. <br /> <br /> That game just looks so fino, even more so if you happen to be a movie and horror sci-fi geek as I am","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-17T09:24:18-07:00","id":1261123,"title":"","content":"I love Boot Hill, finally got my copy yesterday evening!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-20T18:59:21-07:00","id":1261870,"title":"","content":"I am quite happy that I managed to find the missing Elgato box containing the RCA to AV converter cable that I complained about being unable to find in the Hate thread. It turned out to be in my bedside drawer, just underneath one thing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> However, that is only a secondary cause for celebration today; after close to four months of neurotically refusing to use it, I have finally returned to my beloved laptop. More important than that, though, is a complete overhaul to how I am using it.<br /> <br /> For a period of about a year, I had developed an issue of obsessively retaining tabs, often continuously building upon many of them, from the fixation of not being able to let them go until I was satisfied with them, but making them so numerous and deep that doing so became increasingly impractical. Worse than that, it made me terrified of anything, real or imagined, that might cause a reset to my browser in a manner that would cause those tabs to be lost. I would have a single window, set to restore sessions whenever my browser was opened, that would contain dozens of tabs, some of which (especially the YouTube ones) consisting of a backlog of more than a hundred pages.<br /> <br /> That anxiety, combined with some other issues, ultimately created a state in which I couldn't even stand to use it, just leaving it on Standby for weeks at a time; preserving it in state as a shrine to my own madness.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, certain events forced my hand, and I managed to actually go through with something that I've been meaning for ages; to transcribe the contents of those tabs, and then close the extraneous ones. I reduced myself down from fifty tabs to a mere nine, all of which are readily disposed of. I've got everything nicely settled in a manner that I'll never need to have such digital hoarding ever again.<br /> <br /> It's unbelievably liberating. I feel myself as I have not in months, and am able to divest myself of a burdensome habit of a whole chapter of my life. It's delightful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-21T05:38:06-07:00","id":1261925,"title":"","content":"The Hurts Donuts in Fort Worth, TX, is letting customers order donuts to be delivered by a creepy clown with balloons. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-21T13:17:27-07:00","id":12