me Hulk #22 (Weapon H's first full appearance) all graded 9.8.<br /> <br /> I got some more books today. The Return of Wolverine NY Comic Con exclusive glow in the dark cover, a couple of issues of Weapon H to get caught up on the series, and a really nice copy of Rick and Morty #1 (the prices that book goes for are ridonculous).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 11-26-2018, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T18:18:58-08:00","id":1271003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=1270994#post1270994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">CGC Autograph Series 9.8 graded Clayton Crain Weapon H #1 variants, all three versions. I also got a set of the same books unsigned as well as Totally Awesome Hulk #22 (Weapon H's first full appearance) all graded 9.8.<br /> <br /> I got some more books today. The Return of Wolverine NY Comic Con exclusive glow in the dark cover, a couple of issues of Weapon H to get caught up on the series, and a really nice copy of Rick and Morty #1 (the prices that book goes for are ridonculous).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Dude. Niiiiiiice. I'm a big fan of Weapon H. Greg Pak has gone bonkers with a lot of the writing and I'm loving it. I think I have the Dale Keown cover to #1 myself. I like Pak's Roxxon Corporation, which is a heavy influence for Pentex in any WtA games. <br /> <br /> And yeah, Rick and Morty #1 is a hot seller. I wish I jumped on that when I had the chance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T19:10:32-08:00","id":1271010,"title":"","content":"I don't frequently read this genre, but I picked up one of the Chronicles of Darkness fiction anthologies from DTRPG while it was cheap and I found I really loved it. (It was the one that went with Beast, if you're curious.) And then I got the anthology for Mummy, and I've liked that one, too. So now I'm getting most of the rest. So that was an unexpectedly pleasant surprise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T09:34:39-08:00","id":1271471,"title":"","content":"My phone broke last week. I don't have a land line, so I've been unreachable, mostly. That's not a huge problem. Most of my communication is online, anyway. The problem is that, without realizing it, I'd been doing most of my online things using my phone. That's a BIG wrinkle that's annoyed me lately. I'm not usually one to park themselves in front of the computer longer than I absolutely have to. This isn't the Hate Thread, though, and I'm not here to complain. I'll be replacing the phone this week, anyway.<br /> <br /> What I love about this situation is simple: I'm living like I did before smartphones. I'm not glued to a device. I have to actually remember, in detail, something I look up instead of just remembering the gist and trusting the presence of Google in my pocket to handle the rest. It's like my mind is a broken arm that's now healed and out of its cast, with me getting comfortable using it again. It's odd, and temporary, but I'm trying to enjoy this little piece of techlessness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 11-28-2018, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T11:04:02-08:00","id":1271504,"title":"","content":"Creating something that gets an emotional reaction from people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T16:02:00-08:00","id":1271609,"title":"","content":"I love writing poetry. It's such a great way for me to process negative feelings and experiences. I've been distracted from it for a while by so many things, but I'm going to sit down and see if I feel any inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1543-iethloc","name":"Iethloc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1543_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T18:06:44-08:00","id":1271645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=1271003#post1271003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yeah, Rick and Morty #1 is a hot seller. I wish I jumped on that when I had the chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>You and me both. I got it for $250, and that's a relatively low price. I expect the value to at least double once I get it CGC graded. It's in really good condition, I'm thinking 9.4 or higher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T18:41:32-08:00","id":1271654,"title":"","content":"I wrote something about how I look for meaning and safety in other people and how I fall in love too easily, had a cathartic laugh about it... and then was besid myself giddy because a previous date texted me after a bit of radio silence.<br /> <br /> I love knowing myself, for better or worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T23:11:14-08:00","id":1272130,"title":"","content":"A week ago, I had an idea.<br /> <br /> Today, someone I don\u2019t know played my game, had a blast, and cried.<br /> <br /> That feels pretty fucking incredible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T07:30:20-08:00","id":1272175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=1272130#post1272130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A week ago, I had an idea.<br /> <br /> Today, someone I don\u2019t know played my game, had a blast, and cried.<br /> <br /> That feels pretty fucking incredible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Congrats! That's awesome. I read the .docs for <i>Feathers</i> yesterday, and beyond using a system I'm unfamiliar with, it looks absolutely wonderful. I thought about running a short game of it myself once I'm more familiar, as the writeup gave me more than a bit of an idea for a short-run story. Thanks for that!<br /> <br /> On a completely unrelated note: I also love that I got my first full night's sleep in years last night. I should clarify: I got to sleep for the first time in about a decade without heavy medication, and managed to actually rest for hours. This is &quot;when pigs fly&quot; level surprising for me. I sleep like a heard a few too many mortars go off in &quot;the war&quot; ( pick one). PTSD and chronic insomnia are my nearly constant companions, so sleep for me is usually a struggle at best, and nearly always a terrifying experience...but not last night! Nope. I just ran a late session of VtM, finished up, and then nature hit the snooze button. It was great. It might not, probably won't, happen again. I appreciate that it did, though. I love that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T07:23:51-08:00","id":1272617,"title":"","content":"My neighborhood had a blackout last night. After a day of heavy snow. Everything, including the heat, is electric. I was a mess, emotionally. The idea of being cut-off(no phone, either) in the snow, in the dark, made every weird existential anxiety bubble up. Some weird part of me kept thinking &quot;If I die right now, my ghost will never stop screaming&quot;. It lasted for hours.<br /> <br /> ...but,thankfully, I wasn't alone. My girlfriend was right here with me. She was there to hug me when I was shaking from nerves. She helped me distract myself from things by laughing about how imbalanced Mutants &amp; Masterminds is, in her opinion. I agree; I just happen to think it's supposed to be that way. That's besides the point, though. I could have had a terrifying, lonely night in the cold dark of a lonely house. Instead, I spent a few hours being fairly nervous, but in good spirits and better company, until the lights came back and dispelled my fears. I had gotten so used to going through bad things, little (like this) and big, by myself. Being alone with my feelings, my problems, had become the norm for me over the years.<br /> <br /> That's not the case anymore, and I couldn't love that more if I tried. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T21:56:54-08:00","id":1273840,"title":"","content":"Spaghetti Puttanesca. Just recently discovered that this is a thing. It\u2019s a piece of cake to make, and it\u2019s really similar to a sauce my mom used to make, which was my favorite meal growing up. Only this shit is even better! Like, basically the same sauce, but add kalamata olives, red pepper flakes, and swap out the scallops (which kinda suck in Colorado anyway) for anchovies so that seafood taste permeates the whole sauce instead of being in little packets of scallop meat? Yes fucking please!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T18:23:56-08:00","id":1273977,"title":"","content":"I fucking love French onion soup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-12T07:36:23-08:00","id":1274037,"title":"","content":"I love The Simpsons. It was one of my favorite shows from my childhood and still is. When I was a kid back in the late 1990's and early 2000's, Bart Simpson was one of my childhood heroes, right up there with Tuxedo Mask, Mr. Conductor, and Claire Redfield!<br /> <br /> Yeah, I will admit that the more recent seasons aren't very good since Al Jean became the head show runner, but I still love The Simpsons and it is a source of many fond memories of my childhood.<br /> <br /> Hell, my childhood had a lot of awesome shows like The Simpsons, King of the Hill, Digimon, Sailor Moon, and Thomas The Tank Engine/Shining Time Station!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-12T16:32:34-08:00","id":1274114,"title":"","content":"The creative person I look up to the most thought my work was worth sharing.<br /> <br /> C:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edi