isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T05:16:00-08:00","id":1278043,"title":"","content":"Jack: What is that stuff?<br /> Egg Shen: It is black blood of earth.<br /> Jack: You mean oil?<br /> Egg Shen: No, I mean black blood of earth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T02:29:45-08:00","id":1278522,"title":"","content":"I love it when writers deliberately break the &quot;rules&quot; of storytelling.<br /> <br /> I sincerely mean that. Set up a time-honored plot device or theme and then destroy it just for fun. Make the dramatic arc loop back on itself. Set up the Hero, then watch them wink at the camera and cheat through the author's plans. Pick up Chekhov's gun, then shrug and throw it out a window. Iconoclasm is so, so satisfying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","user":"Cielle","date":". 01-04-2019, 05:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T18:23:39-08:00","id":1279359,"title":"","content":"I love The Beatles","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T19:01:16-08:00","id":1279630,"title":"","content":"Really enjoying web serials. Been reading stuff online for decades now but finding <a href=\"https://parahumans.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Worm</a> opened my eyes to some other genres. I tried the writers other work and really couldn't get into it at the time, but it might just take a break from the epic that was Worm. Then there's things like <a href=\"https://www.literotica.com/stories/memberpage.php?uid=1118314&amp;page=submissions\" target=\"_blank\">My Little Ventrue</a> or <a href=\"https://www.royalroad.com/fiction/8894/everybody-loves-large-chests\" target=\"_blank\">Morningwood</a> which are probably more like straight fanfic or porn, and not as mature. But I just found <a href=\"https://wanderinginn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">the Wandering Inn</a>. My first read through hit a block but I came back to it and finished the first 'book' the other night, it's a pretty solid story. I like the way the writer takes a more generic idea (people from the real world fallen into a fantasy RPG one, complete with levels) and spices it up, also focusing on the character and them not being harem-gatherers or chosen ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-08-2019, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T04:17:27-08:00","id":1281275,"title":"","content":"I unironically love Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand.<br /> <br /> It's one of my favorite VTM supplements and does not deserve the hate it gets.<br /> <br /> Other Vampire books I love include The Hunters Hunted, Elysium: The Elder Wars, Chicago by Night 1E, Milwaukee by Night 1E, and Alien Hunger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T09:01:19-08:00","id":1281305,"title":"","content":"Kieron Gillen's DIE is quite good. Might turn out great, but I know for sure I'm loving it so far, both for writing and art.<br /> <br /> The pitch is &quot;Goth Jumanji&quot;. It's about a group of roleplayers in the early 90s (think Masquerade times: Gillen is a fan) who get spirited away into their dark fantasy game and reappear into the world months later, scarred from the experience.<br /> <br /> Years after that, they have to confront the past and return in.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying is that is both something people around here might appreciate and a good source of inspiration for Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T09:42:28-08:00","id":1281312,"title":"","content":"So I've got most of the Pok\u00e9mon to be had from Let's Go Eevee, and was wondering how the heck I'd complete my Pok\u00e9dex without someone to trade with to get a Kabuto. <br /> <br /> That's when I went mucking around in the Cerulean Cave, picking up the random clutter that spawns on the second floor each day, only to find, of all things, a Dome Fossil!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T13:33:58-08:00","id":1281360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_co