ay\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=1285255#post1285255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I'm back. I took some time to think, and I realized something: I'd let other people scare me. Not just scare me, but frighten me away from places I felt safe.<br /> <br /> That I couldn't live with. I am not that b*tch.<br /> <br /> This is where I hang my gaming hat, where my friends are. It's where I belong, and not something people can scare me away from. Not for long. <br /> <br /> It's good to be home.<br /> <br /> - Az</div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome back, Az.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T05:33:21-08:00","id":1285853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=1285733#post1285733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Welcome back, Az.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! Good to be back. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, another thing I love:<br /> <br /> I love horror movies. All kinds of horror, but especially horror with a strong, yet vague, mystical bent. I like being shown magic and miracles without a clear answer as to why things are the way they are. I find that uncertainty inspiring.<br /> <br /> I didn't watch something new, though. I'm just impressed by how moving rewatching <i>Lord of Illusions</i> can be when I keep dozing off and rewinding to previous scenes in case I missed something in a movie I've seen at least 100+ times.<br /> <br /> I thought about about posting this in the movie thread, but <i>Lord of Illusions</i> is already recommended <b>Mage</b> viewing, and this is mostly about me feeling inspired.<br /> <br /> Gonna hack some Mage mechanics today for <b><i>Gemma Mundi</i></b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 02-08-2019, 08:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T08:46:00-08:00","id":1286195,"title":"","content":"I love video games, especially Grand Theft Auto.<br /> <br /> In fact, I recently joined GTA Forums and I've been working on a &quot;concept thread&quot; that basically outlines what my ideal Grand Theft Auto game would look like. It's still a work in progress but I've gotten a lot of work done on it and there are all sorts of in-game weapons, characters (complete with links to images of what I think they would look like), a dream soundtrack spanning a wide variety of genres, a bunch of locations (some return from GTA IV while others are entirely new) and even in-game myths and urban legends (remember how everyone thought Bigfoot was in GTA: San Andreas? In this concept, Bigfoot's actually in the game, along with the Jersey Devil and other weird things)<br /> <br /> The concept is called <b>Grand Theft Auto VI: The Family Secrets </b>and it is a work-in-progress prequel to GTA IV, set in the Northeastern United States during the 1990's and very early 2000's. <br /> <br /> The setting is comprised of three major cities, which are Liberty City (New York City), Keystone City (Philadelphia), and New Plymouth (Boston) and the four regions of Alderney (New Jersey), The Carroways (Long Island), Liberty State (Upstate New York), and New Britannia (New England)<br /> <br /> <br /> I'll post a link to the concept thread. The thread itself has a lot of links, either image links in the case of character images and weaponry images, YouTube links for the songs in the soundtrack, or Wikipedia articles detailing real-life equivalents for the game's locations, in-game media, factions, and myths (for example, clicking on &quot;Liberty City&quot; will link to the Wikipedia page for New York City, &quot;Gambetti Family&quot; links to the page for the Gambino Crime Family, and &quot;The Beast of Alderney&quot; links to the page for the Jersey Devil)<br /> <br /> Here is the link to the concept thread for those interested.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://gtaforums.com/topic/924404-grand-theft-auto-vi-the-family-secrets/\" target=\"_blank\">https://gtaforums.com/topic/924404-g...amily-secrets/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T16:10:48-08:00","id":1286313,"title":"","content":"Sandusky, Ohio, has dropped the holiday celebrating the &quot;accomplishments&quot; of a racist, genocidal buffoon, and has instead made Election Day a paid holiday! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T16:33:49-08:00","id":1286315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=1286313#post1286313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sandusky, Ohio, has dropped the holiday celebrating the &amp;quot;accomplishments&amp;quot; of a racist, genocidal buffoon, and has instead made Election Day a paid holiday! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, nice!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T16:58:12-08:00","id":1286322,"title":"","content":"I've said it once and I'll say it again, but I love sweet tea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T00:51:52-08:00","id":1286637,"title":"","content":"I don't exactly love my current room, but I love having finally been able to assemble my possessions across it in a manner to my liking.<br /> <br /> Especially contrary to the people who insisted that I would not have the space to do so, having seen the way that all of the boxes and bags looked when they were packed filling every space of the room. Ohhh seeing them eat crow is going to be sweet...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T01:31:01-08:00","id":1286643,"title":"","content":"I know I've already said it once, but I will say it again.<br /> <br /> I love my little creative concept project that I've been working on and having a lot of fun with. It's kind of neat to write up and outline your ideal video game from your favorite franchise. Again, I will link the concept below because I have made some massive updates to it.<br /> <a href=\"https://gtaforums.com/topic/924404-grand-theft-auto-vi-the-family-secrets/\" target=\"_blank\">https://gtaforums.com/topic/924404-g...amily-secrets/</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T12:39:24-08:00","id":1287191,"title":"","content":"I love that my gaming muse seems to be coming back. I've been listening to the same set of songs for months (thanks to my toddler, my music catalog had to be seriously limited), but yesterday those same songs introduced me to a set of NPCs for a game I'm planning to run and gave me a fairly kick-ass vibe for that game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24219-goddessgood","name":"goddessgood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T14:06:10-08:00","id":1288727,"title":"","content":"I love the fan characters I've been creating for Grand Theft Auto. I'm using a Sailor Moon OC Maker game to create the images of these GTA OC's.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T00:01:39-08:00","id":1288863,"title":"","content":"After more than five years without it, I might finally have a shot at regular tabletop gaming face to face again. Don't get me wrong, Discord is a godsend, but\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-17-2019, 06:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T20:54:39-08:00","id":1289405,"title":"","content":"Found my Dad's stash of comics that were left for me after he passed. Lots of gems, here.<br /> <br /> And I'll never sell them. Just pass them down to my own son.<br /> <br /> R.I.P. Dad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 02-25-2019, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T14:04:58-08:00","id":1290098,"title":"","content":"I work for an international company. Most of my coworkers are in the UK, but me and my team are US-based. Today I learned that the phrase &quot;fancy dress party&quot; means completely different things on either side of the pond. In the US it indicates formal wear is required, you go in your Sunday best. In the UK, it means something more like a funny costume party. You'd dress up as Fred Flintstone or a comic book hero. Thinking about that made me smile when I really needed it today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24219-goddessgood","name":"goddessgood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T14:41:25-08:00","id":1291960,"title":"","content":"I love being able to meet Steve Jackson this past weekend at MystiCon 2019.<br /> <br /> He's a great dude, very laid-back when I met him, despite his esteemed reputation in the gaming hobby.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T17:32:58-08:00","id":1292302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/895314-whete-do-kindred-get-money-from?p=895815#post895815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most vampires engage in the world's oldest profession.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/895314-whete-do-kindred-get-money-from?p=896459#post896459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mammoth hunting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got reminded of this and giggled again. Yes, I laugh at my own jokes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T12:57:17-08:00","id":1293340,"title":"","content":"Reading through Wraith: Charnel Houses of Europe. It's been over a decade since I read through it the last time. <br /> <br /> God, it's so, SO good. And Important. And sad. But people, THIS is what RPG books can be. Intelligent, meaningful, real and can also be a hell of a resource at the gaming table.<br /> <br /> This is the World of Darkness done right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T08:52:54-07:00","id":1296149,"title":"","content":"I love the fact that I am actually designing my own custom RPG system from scratch.<br /> <br /> Not an OSR clone, but an actual new system, it's a simple percentile system based on d10's and d100's and is intended for survival sandbox game play.<br /> <br /> I've even been working on some custom settings for it, including fairy tale fantasy and post-apocalyptic horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T02:42:00-07:00","id":1296634,"title":"","content":"I love the new Lunars book - you can face your enemies in the form of a dog with bees in your mouth, so when you bark, you shoot bees at them!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby