ount":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T19:09:34-07:00","id":1394931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NotEmpathic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=1394921#post1394921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secret ballots, and I don't think everyone will look at it like that. Most people just want the chaos to stop, and disbanding police won't achieve that...</div> </div> </div> </div>The most peaceful protests have been those with no police there to escalate. Evidence shows people only really freak out and start wrecking shit when the authorities are brutalizing people.<br /> <br /> Who knew?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T19:47:55-07:00","id":1394939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NotEmpathic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=1394921#post1394921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secret ballots, and I don't think everyone will look at it like that. Most people just want the chaos to stop, and disbanding police won't achieve that...</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't address the issue.<br /> <br /> Everyone wants this to stop. The most powerful Republicans are either suggesting stopping it through more police violence, or ducking cameras and reporters to avoid saying anything on the record. The Democrats are suggesting, with plenty of disagreement between prominent Democrats on how, reform and increased oversight of the police system to stop the &quot;chaos&quot; by ending the reason it exists.<br /> <br /> All polling so far suggests that America is increasingly against the &quot;law and order, more cops with more power,&quot; approach; which is the most loud voice solution within the Republican party.<br /> <br /> Why would this grow the Republican base?<br /> <br /> Why are more people going to look at the Republicans and go, &quot;this is the party were a white Senator from Kentucky tried to stop a bipartisan anti-lynching bill and tried to lecture two Senators of color about the history of lynching on the Senatre floor,&quot; so they clearly know how to rebuild the trust between the police and the black community?<br /> <br /> Why are people going to join the Republican party, that kicked out a rather far right Libertarian Congressman that was actually willing to put a bill to the House that could easily get Democratic support because it would actually help? Kicking out a guy with a bipartisan appealing solution to at least part of the chaos is supposed to appeal to people that aren't already loyal Republicans? How?<br /> <br /> Who are the voters that were thinking, &quot;You know, I wasn't going to vote Republican, but they clearly have the right solution to end this?&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T22:57:10-07:00","id":1395011,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://twitter.com/ACLUMN/status/1269738051498106880?s=19\" target=\"_blank\">Minneapolis has announced they intend to disband their police department.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-08-2020, 02:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T02:36:28-07:00","id":1395273,"title":"","content":"As of the time I\u2019m writing this, the Seattle East Precinct that the police abandoned earlier in the day has not only not been burned down, it\u2019s been turned into a peaceful commune.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link"