mPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-25T18:24:45-07:00","id":1493697,"title":"","content":"We watched The Pelican Brief on Netflix, which I had seen on VCR. It's a classic suspense film with an environmental theme. Julia Roberts' voice is super soft in parts of the movie, causing me to turn up the volume. Then, there's the car-bombs and car chases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-01T08:59:19-07:00","id":1494089,"title":"","content":"I remember The Pelican Brief when it first came out. It's was Julia Roberts first major film after a short 2 or three year break from acting and strangely I didn't have a problem with her soft voice back then and I didn't need to adjust the volume. Of course now I might have to do it now due to some mild hearing loss in my left ear and I find it hard to understand what Colin Farrell says when he speaks in a much stronger Irish accent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-01T12:29:28-07:00","id":1494107,"title":"","content":"Some recent discussion of Pentex had me thinking of Pelican Brief and Erin Brockovich, another movie in which she investigates powerful people for greed at the expense of the environment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-02T13:11:26-07:00","id":1494148,"title":"","content":"Julia Roberts made some really good movies in the 1990\u2019s. Erin Brocovich was another gem of her acting range.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-12T11:46:17-07:00","id":1494879,"title":"","content":"I an traveling down to Georgia rn and I am actually glad I missed yesterday's Amtrak train. It gave me time to relax and it meant I met this old man named John while waiting to board today's Auto Train. And he has had a fascinating life. I love talking with him","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-13T14:52:26-07:00","id":1494941,"title":"","content":"I was able to find season eight of Dr. House at long last and I've completed the collection of this series today.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-20T20:28:13-07:00","id":1495342,"title":"","content":"I can't believe I'm about to do this. There is an almost EIGHT HOUR <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VeH7qKZr0WI\" target=\"_blank\">episode</a> of Lex Fridman where he interviews Balaji Srinivasan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-09T18:16:11-08:00","id":1496666,"title":"","content":"The visual effects applied to the portrait of a woman on <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7ump3I2mviY\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> binaural beats video. Her deep blue eyes have a milky blur. Matching blue mascara only under one eye moves in a sort of circular motion. There are more things moving, which I will leave for anyone to see how many you can pick out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-18T09:44:49-08:00","id":1497466,"title":"","content":"I love seeing the GOP fall into rancorous, internecine dissent over how badly the country just rejected their special brand of lunacy and its attempt to claim the senate in the primaries. I relish the way they immediately reverted to type in the house with their narrow victory and tried to devolve into chasing ignorant conspiracy theories instead of actually legislating. I especially enjoy them making cheap excuses to cover their obvious failings, blaming the youth of america (basically anyone 18-30) who turned out in droves to NOT vote for them.<br /> <br /> It amuses me greatly to see that trump\u2019s assumed golden touch in politics has turned into &quot;wyrm-taint&quot; that makes candidates anathema and drags the party into the dust. I chuckle at how the evangelical cultists who thought to follow trumps coattails into power are even now trying to say he \u201cused\u201d them, or \u201cbetrayed\u201d them, when it was their obvious intent to turn this nation into a backwards theocracy. Now that their pipe-dreams are shattered we can get back to flipping the bird to their obnoxiously intolerant, judgmental little sub-sect.<br /> <br /> I can't wait for them to self-destruct on live TV<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-18T13:21:32-08:00","id":1497481,"title":"","content":"Honestly, while I'm going to enjoy the House Republicans fail to learn the message of this year that the center-right of the country is done with catering to the far-right nonsense in one level, I can't love it because there's a lot of stuff that needs to get done ASAP, that isn't going to happen for at least two more years of gridlock. If they were going to do basic governing issues, let alone get on solving real problems everyone agrees are problems and need fixing, and then waste time on Hunter Biden's laptop? Whatever. That they're going to act like &quot;solving&quot; Hunter Biden's laptop is more important than keeping the lights on is something that hurts a lot of people.<br /> <br /> If there's something to really love out of the leadership changes after the last election, it's watching Pelosi bow out with actual style and grace Love her, hate her, everyone should be able to respect her stepping down when it's clear her era is over, and handing things over to the next generation of leaders in her party. No infighting, no drama, no prying power from her cold dead hands; just a politician that can actually see that it's time to cede control to others because it's the right time to pass the torch.<br /> <br /> I hope everyone with power, not just politicians, and not just Americans, can watch her speech and remember the simple point that if you've used your power well, you can let it go with confidence that what you built will be in good hands without you in charge; and that's the best way to step out of the spotlight.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-18T18:24:13-08:00","id":1497501,"title":"","content":"I had not seen Pelosi's speech before Trump's speech announcing a third try for the White House, in which he claimed credit for &quot;firing&quot; her. There were other things he said that seemed to lack grammatical and logical sense. When I searched for Pelosi's speech, among the top results, Canadian outlet Global News was the one who gave the longest coverage, about 45 minutes. One American outlet's coverage was just over 1 minute long. So I watched the Global one. She has a nice laugh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-18T20:25:37-08:00","id":1497505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=1497466#post1497466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't wait for them to self-destruct on live TV</div> </div> </div> </div>The next two years will be very interesting. After basically &quot;losing&quot; 3 times (2018 midterms, 2020 and now in 2022) there's a lot of Republicans who are starting to realize that Donald Trump is an albatross. He's great at getting people out to vote... for the Democrats. His defeating Hillary was kind of a fluke because she was one of the only people more widely disliked than Trump was, and even then it was a close win.<br /> <br /> And the thing is, the Republicans actually did relatively well this year, at least the more moderate, middle of the road ones. But the crazy election deniers and the ones closest to Trump ended up losing. If the Republicans had just stuck to running more standard candidates, they would have probably would have been able to take the Senate. Instead they ended up with people like Oz and Walker and failed as a result. And that's despite the massive gerrymandering and attempts to making voting harder.<br /> <br /> Of course, what's going to happen in 2024? If Trump wins the nomination, and it's possible he will because he still has a sizeable base in the Republican Party that will vote for him no matter what, then it's very likely that the Republicans will again not do very well in the general election. But if he doesn't win the Republican nomination because the Republicans vote for someone who would do better in a general election like DeSantis, then there's a high chance he'll run as an independent, or tell his fans to stay home, and take the Republican party down with him out of spite.<br /> <br /> They're very much stuck between a rock and a hard place. And the thing is, Trump could just keep running again and again, either as the Republican nominee or as an independent and you could see the Republican Party performing poorly in general elections for a decade or more as a result.<br /> <br /> The Republicans could have avoided all of that by voting to impeach him after January 6th but, oops.<br /> <br /> Still, a lot could happen in 2 years and there's no telling where things will be. Things could start getting so bad that a majority of Americans could end up feeling that seeing Trump and the Republicans back in power is better than the alternative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 11-19-2022, 01:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-19T04:59:49-08:00","id":1497525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3535-you-know-what-i-love-mk-i?p=1497505#post1497505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The next two years will be very interesting. After basically &amp;quot;losing&amp;quot; 3 times (2018 midterms, 2020 and now in 2022) there's a lot of Republicans who are starting to realize that Donald Trump is an albatross. He's great at getting people out to vote... for the Democrats. His defeating Hillary was kind of a fluke because she was one of the only people more widely disliked than Trump was, and even then it was a close win.<br /> <br /> And the thing is, the Republicans actually did relatively well this year, at least the more moderate, middle of the road ones. But the crazy election deniers and the ones closest to Trump ended up losing. If the Republicans had just stuck to running more standard candidates, they would have probably would have been able to take the Senate. Instead they ended up with people like Oz and Walker and failed as a result. And that's despite the massive gerrymandering and attempts to making voting harder.<br /> <br /> Of course, what's going to happen in 2024? If Trump wins the nomination, and it's possible he will because he still has a sizeable base in the Republican Party that will vote for him no matter what, then it's very likely that the Republicans will again not do very well in the general election. But if he doesn't win the Republican nomination because the Republicans vote for someone who would do better in a general election like DeSantis, then there's a high chance he'll run as an independent, or tell his fans to stay home, and take the Republican party down with him out of spite.<br /> <br /> They're very much stuck between a rock and a hard place. And the thing is, Trump could just keep running again and again, either as the Republican nominee or as an independent and you could see the Republican Party performing poorly in general elections for a decade or more as a result.<br /> <br /> The Republicans could have avoided all of that by voting to impeach him after January 6th but, oops.<br /> <br /> Still, a lot could happen in 2 years and there's no telling where things will be. Things could start getting so bad that a majority of Americans could end up feeling that seeing Trump and the Republicans back in power is better than the alternative.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with your analysis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-19T09:49:15-08:00","id":1497533,"title":"","content":"I'm starting to get into South Korean action films recently and gives me hope that storytelling in movies isn't quite as dead as I feared it was and my friend is already recommending movies for me to check out.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-19T09:52:04-08:00","id":1497534,"title":"","content":"I'm also find Elon Musk takeover of Twitter entertaining as people are losing there minds of how there platform is being managed and rules could be enforced as folks like Kathy Griffth learned.